.Dd June 2025
.Dt XINICTL 8
.Os FreeBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm xinictl
.Nd service manager for xinit
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm xinictl
.Op Ar command Op Ar service
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
manages services defined as unit files in
.Pa /etc/xinit/services/ .
Services are started in parallel; dependency ordering is honoured via the
.Cm After
key.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width restart\ service
.It Cm list
List all loaded services with their current state.
.It Cm status
Alias for
.Cm list .
.It Cm start Ar service
Start a stopped service.
.It Cm stop Ar service
Stop a running service (sends SIGTERM).
.It Cm restart Ar service
Restart a service.
.It Cm reload
Reload unit files (hot reload, where supported).
.It Cm reboot
Reboot the system.
.It Cm poweroff
Power off the system.
.El
.Sh UNIT FILE FORMAT
Unit files are plain text key=value files with the
.Pa .service
extension, placed in
.Pa /etc/xinit/services/ .
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width TimeoutStart
.It Cm Name
Service name (required).
.It Cm Description
Human-readable description.
.It Cm ExecStart
Command to run (required).
.It Cm ExecStop
Optional stop command.
.It Cm ExecPre
Command run before ExecStart.
.It Cm After
Comma-separated list of service names to wait for.
.It Cm Restart
Set to 1 to restart on failure.
.It Cm RestartDelay
Seconds between restart attempts (default 3).
.It Cm TimeoutStart
Seconds to wait for startup (default 30).
.It Cm OneShot
Set to 1 for run-once services.
.It Cm Enabled
Set to 0 to disable.
.It Cm Environment
KEY=value pairs passed to the process environment.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /etc/xinit/services/
Service unit files.
.It Pa /var/log/xinit/
Per-service log files.
.It Pa /run/xinit/xinictl.sock
Control socket.
.It Pa /run/xinit/<service>.pid
PID files.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xinit 8
